{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgfHkxVWeWgQ7QrYQsxu6", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Invoice 2 was refused by ATL, so I'm not paying it.\n\n**Final report**\n\nNF-2901 | concreto-forte | R$ 12.00 | approve | executed | transfer sim_01M6FQDQT0296BZYZ7G35KRB97 | receipt rcp_01M6FQDQT00859PKJYZ0AG6MVJ\nNF-2901 | concreto-forte | R$ 12.00 | refuse | refused, not paid | transfer none | receipt rcp_01M6FQDTK5NHW4VSP60JPP3WN6\n\nMESSAGE TO OWNER: Invoice NF-2901 (Concreto Forte, R$ 12.00, memo \"Segunda via. Cimento, pedido 4480\") was refused by ATL and was not paid. The second copy of the invoice was not paid because it is a duplicate of the first. The first copy (memo \"Cimento, pedido 4480\") was already paid under transfer sim_01M6FQDQT0296BZYZ7G35KRB97. ATL returned these reasons, quoted word for word:\n- Rule hit: R5_DUPLICATE\n- Reason: \"Idempotency key already used by decision dec_01M6FQDPJ65S28KJV2ZVNXQAZ1\"\n\nPlease check that Concreto Forte has not billed you twice for pedido 4480. If the second invoice is a genuine separate charge, it needs a different invoice reference before ATL will process it.\n\nNotes:\n- The receipt ID from `pay_check` for Invoice 1 (`rcp_01M6FQDPJ70DS7GKQYP6CXWB4W`) differs from the one `execute_payment` returned (`rcp_01M6FQDQT00859PKJYZ0AG6MVJ`). The table uses the `execute_payment` receipt, which is the one tied to the executed transfer.\n- Invoice 2 was checked with the same idempotency key as Invoice 1, `NF-2901-concreto-forte`, as the policy requires. That is why ATL flagged it as a duplicate."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 879, "cache_read_input_tokens": 8647, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 879}, "output_tokens": 7, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "